    "The road beyond Ayodhya was no longer a road of celebration. Rama, Sita and Lakshmana had left behind the city, the palace, the crown that had never been placed upon Rama's head, and the people who had followed them until they could go no farther. Ahead lay forests, rivers and hermitages unknown to Sita, but Rama walked without resentment, carrying his father's word as the one thing he refused to abandon.",

