        `Before boarding, Sita folded her hands toward the river and offered a silent prayer for their safe passage. Lakshmana helped her into the boat, then stepped aboard himself. Rama took one last look at Guha. The Nishada king stood at the edge of the water, watching them with affection and sorrow. Neither man tried to prolong the farewell. The river waited before them, and the journey had to continue.`
