        `Rama lowered his eyes, moved by the distinction she had made. "I sometimes worry that my decision has taken away the life you deserved." Sita turned toward him. "You cannot decide what my life should mean without listening to me. I had a home in Mithila, and I found another in Ayodhya. Now I am learning how to make a home here. It is not the life I imagined, but it is still my life, and I have chosen to share it with you."`,

        `When they resumed their journey, Rama walked at a pace that allowed them to travel comfortably together. Lakshmana moved ahead when the path required it, then returned to check on them. The forest was still unfamiliar, and the road was long, but the three began to discover a rhythm that belonged to them alone. Their circumstances had changed, yet small moments of humour, honesty and care remained possible.`
